<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>io.github.zednaked.Nirbija</id>
  <name>Nirbija</name>
  <summary>A mixer that is also an instrument</summary>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0-only</project_license>
  <developer id="io.github.zednaked">
    <name>Thiago Gonçalves</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>
      A rack of channel strips for Linux, in the spirit of AUM on iOS. Each
      strip is a chain: an instrument, then effects, then a fader with sends.
      A drone synth, a sixteen-pad sampler, a looper, a step sequencer and an
      arpeggiator ship inside the binary, and LV2, CLAP and VST3 plugins go in
      the same slot, over JACK or PipeWire, with their own editors embedded.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every control answers a drag, the wheel and the keyboard. The whole
      interface is sized off one number, remembered per machine.
    </p>
  </description>
